<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand de Lesseps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1805–1894</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand de Lesseps was a French diplomat and entrepreneur who developed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a>, opened in 1869. Encouraged by that success, he launched a French company to build a sea-level canal across Panama in 1881, but disease, landslides and engineering problems overwhelmed the project, which collapsed in 1889 after many thousands of workers had died. The bankruptcy caused a great political scandal in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in which he was convicted, though the sentence was later quashed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-de-lesseps.jpg" alt="Ferdinand de Lesseps" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_de_Lesseps_by_Nadar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
